#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.47 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:9
msgid ""
"Many Porcelain commands that internally use the merge machinery were taught "
"to consistently honor the diff.algorithm configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:11
msgid "A few descriptions in \"git show-ref -h\" have been clarified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:14
msgid ""
"A 'P' command to \"git add -p\" that passes the patch hunk to the pager has "
"been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:18
msgid ""
"\"git grep -W\" omits blank lines that follow the found function at the end "
"of the file, just like it omits blank lines before the next function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:23
msgid ""
"The value of http.proxy can have \"path\" at the end for a socks proxy that "
"listens to a unix-domain socket, but we started to discard it when we taught "
"proxy auth code path to use the credential helpers, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:27
msgid ""
"The code paths to compact multiple reftable files have been updated to "
"correctly deal with multiple compaction triggering at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:29
msgid "Support to specify ref backend for submodules has been enhanced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:32
msgid ""
"\"git svn\" has been taught about svn:global-ignores property recent "
"versions of Subversion has."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:37
msgid ""
"The default object hash and ref backend format used to be settable only with "
"explicit command line option to \"git init\" and environment variables, but "
"now they can be configured in the user's global and system wide "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:41
msgid ""
"\"git send-email\" learned \"--translate-aliases\" option that reads "
"addresses from the standard input and emits the result of applying aliases "
"on them to the standard output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:45
msgid ""
"'git for-each-ref' learned a new \"--format\" atom to find the branch that "
"the history leading to a given commit \"%(is-base:<commit>)\" is likely "
"based on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:48
msgid ""
"The command line prompt support used to be littered with bash-isms, which "
"has been corrected to work with more shells."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:50
msgid "Support for the RUNTIME_PREFIX feature has been added to z/OS port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:53
msgid ""
"\"git send-email\" learned \"--mailmap\" option to allow rewriting the "
"recipient addresses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:55
msgid "\"git mergetool\" learned to use VSCode as a merge backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:57
msgid "\"git pack-redundant\" has been marked for removal in Git 3.0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:61
msgid ""
"One-line messages to \"die\" and other helper functions will get LF added by "
"these helper functions, but many existing messages had an unnecessary LF at "
"the end, which have been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:63
msgid "The \"scalar clone\" command learned the \"--no-tags\" option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:67
msgid ""
"The environment GIT_ADVICE has been intentionally kept undocumented to "
"discourage its use by interactive users.  Add documentation to help tool "
"writers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:69
msgid "\"git apply --3way\" learned to take \"--ours\" and other options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:76
msgid ""
"A build tweak knob has been simplified by not setting the value that is "
"already the default; another unused one has been removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:79
msgid ""
"A CI job that use clang-format to check coding style issues in new code has "
"been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:82
msgid ""
"The reviewing guidelines document now explicitly encourages people to give "
"positive reviews and how."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:86
msgid ""
"Test script linter has been updated to catch an attempt to use one-shot "
"export construct \"VAR=VAL func\" for shell functions (which does not work "
"for some shells) better."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:88
msgid "Some project conventions have been added to CodingGuidelines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:92
msgid ""
"In the refs subsystem, implicit reliance of the_repository has been "
"eliminated; the repository associated with the ref store object is used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:95
msgid ""
"Various tests in reftable library have been rewritten using the unit test "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:99
msgid ""
"A test that fails on an unusually slow machine was found, and made less "
"likely to cause trouble by lengthening the expiry value it uses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:102
msgid ""
"An existing test of hashmap API has been rewritten with the unit-test "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:105
msgid ""
"A policy document that describes platform support levels and expectation on "
"platform stakeholders has been introduced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:109
msgid ""
"The refs API has been taught to give symref target information to the users "
"of ref iterators, allowing for-each-ref and friends to avoid an extra "
"ref_resolve_* API call per a symbolic ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:113
msgid ""
"Unit-test framework has learned a simple control structure to allow "
"embedding test statements in-line instead of having to create a new function "
"to contain them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:115
msgid "Incremental updates of multi-pack index files is getting worked on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:119
msgid ""
"Use of API functions that implicitly depend on the_repository object in the "
"config subsystem has been rewritten to pass a repository object through the "
"callchain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:122
msgid ""
"Unused parameters have been either marked as UNUSED to squelch -Wunused "
"warnings or dropped from many functions.."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:125
msgid ""
"The code in the reftable library has been cleaned up by discarding unused "
"\"generic\" interface."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:129
msgid ""
"The underlying machinery for \"git diff-index\" has long been made to expand "
"the sparse index as needed, but the command fully expanded the sparse index "
"upfront, which now has been taught not to do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:132
msgid ""
"More trace2 events at key points on push and fetch code paths have been "
"added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:135
msgid "Make our codebase compilable with the -Werror=unused-parameter option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:138
msgid "\"git cat-file\" works well with the sparse-index, and gets marked as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:142
msgid ""
"CI started failing completely for linux32 jobs, as the step to upload failed "
"test directory uses GitHub actions that is deprecated and is now disabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:145
msgid "Import clar unit tests framework libgit2 folks invented for our use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:147
msgid "The error messages from the test script checker have been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:151
msgid ""
"The convention to calling into built-in command implementation has been "
"updated to pass the repository, if known, together with the prefix value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:155
msgid ""
"\"git apply\" had custom buffer management code that predated before use of "
"strbuf got widespread, which has been updated to use strbuf, which also "
"plugged some memory leaks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:158
msgid ""
"The reftable backend learned to more efficiently handle exclude patterns "
"while enumerating the refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:161
msgid ""
"CI updates.  FreeBSD image has been updated to 13.4.  (merge 2eeb29702e "
"cb/ci-freebsd-13-4 later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:164
msgid ""
"Give timeout to the locking code to write to reftable, instead of failing on "
"the first failure without retrying."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:169
msgid ""
"The checksum at the tail of files are now computed without collision "
"detection protection.  This is safe as the consumer of the information to "
"protect itself from replay attacks checks for hash collisions independently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.46"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:178
msgid ""
"\"git add -p\" by users with diff.suppressBlankEmpty set to true failed to "
"parse the patch that represents an unmodified empty line with an empty line "
"(not a line with a single space on it), which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:183
msgid ""
"\"git checkout --ours\" (no other arguments) complained that the option is "
"incompatible with branch switching, which is technically correct, but found "
"confusing by some users.  It now says that the user needs to give pathspec "
"to specify what paths to checkout."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:185
msgid "It has been documented that we avoid \"VAR=VAL shell_func\" and why."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:189
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --help\" referred to \"offset\" (the difference between the "
"location a change was taken from and the change gets replaced)  incorrectly "
"and called it \"fuzz\", which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:193
msgid ""
"\"git notes add -m '' --allow-empty\" and friends that take prepared data to "
"create notes should not invoke an editor, but it started doing so since Git "
"2.42, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:197
msgid ""
"An expensive operation to prepare tracing was done in re-encoding code path "
"even when the tracing was not requested, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:199
msgid "More leakfixes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:202
msgid ""
"The credential helper to talk to OSX keychain sometimes sent garbage bytes "
"after the username, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:205
msgid ""
"A recent update broke \"git ls-remote\" used outside a repository, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:208
msgid ""
"The patch parser in 'git apply' has been a bit more lenient against "
"unexpected mode bits, like 100664, recorded on extended header lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:212
msgid ""
"\"git config --value=foo --fixed-value section.key newvalue\" barfed when "
"the existing value in the configuration file used the valueless true syntax, "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:216
msgid ""
"The patch parser in \"git patch-id\" has been tightened to avoid getting "
"confused by lines that look like a patch header in the log message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:219
msgid ""
"\"git reflog expire\" failed to honor annotated tags when computing "
"reachable commits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:222
msgid "A flakey test and incorrect calls to strtoX() functions have been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:224
msgid "Follow-up on 2.45.1 regression fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:228
msgid ""
"\"git rev-list ... | git diff-tree -p --remerge-diff --stdin\" should behave "
"more or less like \"git log -p --remerge-diff\" but instead it crashed, "
"forgetting to prepare a temporary object store needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:231
msgid ""
"\"git bundle unbundle\" outside a repository triggered a BUG()  "
"unnecessarily, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:234
msgid ""
"Maintenance tasks other than \"gc\" now properly go background when \"git "
"maintenance\" runs them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:239
msgid ""
"We created a useless pseudo-merge reachability bitmap that is about 0 "
"commits, and attempted to include commits that are not in packs, which made "
"no sense.  These bugs have been corrected.  (merge a72dfab8b8 "
"tb/pseudo-merge-bitmap-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:241
msgid "\"git rebase -x --quiet\" was not quiet, which was corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:244
msgid ""
"The code path for compacting reftable files saw some bugfixes against "
"concurrent operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:248
msgid ""
"The code forgot to discard unnecessary in-core commit buffer data for "
"commits that \"git log --skip=<number>\" traversed but omitted from the "
"output, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:251
msgid ""
"\"git verify-pack\" and \"git index-pack\" started dying outside a "
"repository, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:254
msgid ""
"A data corruption bug when multi-pack-index is used and the same objects are "
"stored in multiple packfiles has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:258
msgid ""
"\"git pack-refs --auto\" for the files backend was too aggressive, which has "
"been a bit tamed.  (merge c3459ae9ef ps/pack-refs-auto-heuristics later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:261
msgid ""
"A file descriptor left open is now properly closed when \"git "
"sparse-checkout\" updates the sparse patterns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:265
msgid ""
"In a few corner cases \"git diff --exit-code\" failed to report \"changes\" "
"(e.g., renamed without any content change), which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:268
msgid ""
"Cygwin does have /dev/tty support that is needed by things like single-key "
"input mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:271
msgid ""
"The interpret-trailers command failed to recognise the end of the message "
"when the commit log ends in an incomplete line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:276
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --autostash\" failed to resurrect the autostashed changes when "
"the command gets aborted after giving back control asking for hlep in "
"conflict resolution.  (merge bf6ab087d1 pw/rebase-autostash-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:280
msgid ""
"The \"imap-send\" now allows to be compiled with NO_OPENSSL and OPENSSL_SHA1 "
"defined together.  (merge 997950a750 jk/no-openssl-with-openssl-sha1 later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:284
msgid ""
"The support to customize build options to adjust for older versions and/or "
"older systems for the interop tests has been improved.  (merge 22ef5f02a8 "
"jk/interop-test-build-options later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:287
msgid ""
"Update the character width table for Unicode 16.  (merge 44dc651132 "
"bb/unicode-width-table-16 later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:291
msgid ""
"In Git 2.39, Git.pm stopped working in a bare repository, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge d3edb0bdde jk/git-pm-bare-repo-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:296
msgid ""
"When a remote-helper dies before Git writes to it, SIGPIPE killed Git "
"silently.  We now explain the situation a bit better to the end user in our "
"error message.  (merge 6e7fac9bca jk/diag-unexpected-remote-helper-death "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:299
msgid ""
"A few usability fixes to \"git jump\" (in contrib/).  (merge 083b82544d "
"jk/jump-quickfix-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:303
msgid ""
"\"git diff --exit-code\" ignored modified binary files, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge 9a41735af6 rs/diff-exit-code-binary later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:309
msgid ""
"When a subprocess to work in a submodule spawned by \"git submodule\" fails "
"with SIGPIPE, the parent Git process caught the death of it, but gave a "
"generic \"failed to work in that submodule\", which was misleading.  We now "
"behave as if the parent got SIGPIPE and die.  (merge 082caf527e "
"pw/submodule-process-sigpipe later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:313
msgid ""
"\"git archive\" with pathspec magic that uses the attribute information did "
"not work well, which has been corrected.  (merge 296743a7ca "
"rs/archive-with-attr-pathspec-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:320
msgid ""
"Background tasks \"git maintenance\" runs may need to use credential "
"information when going over the network, but a credential helper may work "
"only in an interactive environment, and end up blocking a scheduled task "
"waiting for UI.  Credential helpers can now behave differently when they are "
"not running interactively.  (merge b9183b0a02 "
"ds/background-maintenance-with-credential later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:324
msgid ""
"\"git --git-dir=nowhere cmd\" failed to properly notice that it wasn't in "
"any repository while processing includeIf.onbranch configuration and instead "
"crashed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:330
msgid ""
"When \"git sparse-checkout disable\" turns a sparse checkout into a regular "
"checkout, the index is fully expanded.  This totally expected behaviour "
"however had an \"oops, we are expanding the index\" advice message, which "
"has been corrected.  (merge 537e516a39 ds/sparse-checkout-expansion-advice "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:333
msgid ""
"macOS with fsmonitor daemon can hang forever when a submodule is involved, "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.47.0.txt:342
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge be10ac7037 "
"jc/mailinfo-header-cleanup later to maint).  (merge 4460e052e0 "
"jc/range-diff-lazy-setup later to maint).  (merge 0627c58e7a ak/typofixes "
"later to maint).  (merge 83799f1500 jk/t9001-deflake later to maint).  "
"(merge e02cc08a88 ak/typofix-2.46-maint later to maint).  (merge 5c5d29e1c4 "
"ps/ci-gitlab-upgrade later to maint).  (merge 9c4c840901 "
"jc/doc-discarding-stalled-topics later to maint).  (merge 5e6f359f6b "
"ds/read-cache-mempool-leakfix later to maint)."
msgstr ""
